        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'PRESSURE DATUMS\n\n  p_abs  =  p_gauge  +  p_atm\n\n  p_abs   >= 0 ALWAYS (measured from perfect vacuum)\n  p_gauge can be negative (= "vacuum pressure")\n\n  p_atm at sea level = 101.325 kPa = 760 mm Hg\n                     = 10.33 m of water\n\nWORKED: condenser reads 700 mm Hg VACUUM,\n        barometer reads 760 mm Hg\n\n  p_abs = 760 - 700 = 60 mm Hg\n        = 0.060 * 13600 * 9.81\n        = 8.00 kPa ABSOLUTE\n\n  (NOT "-93 kPa" when compared with vapour pressure)\n\nUSE ABSOLUTE FOR:\n  gas laws, vapour pressure / cavitation,\n  compressible flow, any thermodynamics.\n\nUSE GAUGE FOR:\n  structural loads, manometry, most pipe flow.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.3, pp.59-61 (8th ed.).' },
