    notes:
      'Built from TB1 Chapters 2, 5, 6 and 8, taken in the order the syllabus lists rather than the order the book presents, because the syllabus places the kinematic description before the dynamics of Module 3. The organising idea is that kinematics is description without cause: nothing in this module asks what force drives the flow, only what shapes the flow can take and what constraints it must satisfy. Continuity is the single constraint, and the stream function and velocity potential are devices for satisfying it automatically. The laminar flow solutions at the end are included because they are the only exact solutions students will meet, and because the syllabus explicitly names power absorbed in bearings, which the book treats through these same solutions. All page numbers are 8th-edition pages.',
