        terms: ['stream function', 'two dimensional flow', 'automatic continuity', 'constant along streamline', 'volume flow rate'],
        definition:
          'The stream function is a single scalar function defined for two dimensional incompressible flow such that the velocity components are obtained by differentiating it, the x component being the derivative with respect to y and the y component the negative derivative with respect to x. Defined this way it satisfies continuity identically, because the mixed second derivatives cancel whatever function is chosen, so two unknowns are replaced by one that automatically obeys mass conservation. It has two further properties that make it indispensable: it is constant along any streamline, so lines of constant stream function are the streamlines themselves, and the difference in its value between two streamlines equals the volume flow rate between them.',
        takeaway: 'The stream function satisfies continuity automatically, its contours are the streamlines, and its differences are flow rates.',
