        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'STREAM FUNCTION  psi(x,y)\n\nDEFINED SO THAT:\n\n  u = + d(psi)/dy\n  v = - d(psi)/dx\n\nWHY THAT DEFINITION:\n\n  du/dx + dv/dy\n    = d2(psi)/dxdy - d2(psi)/dydx\n    = 0            IDENTICALLY, for ANY psi\n\n  -> continuity is satisfied AUTOMATICALLY\n  -> 2 unknowns (u,v) replaced by 1 unknown (psi)\n\nTWO MORE PROPERTIES:\n\n  psi = constant  ->  that curve IS a streamline\n  psi_2 - psi_1   ->  volume flow rate BETWEEN them\n                      (per unit depth)\n\nWORKED: psi = 3xy\n\n  u = d(3xy)/dy = 3x\n  v = -d(3xy)/dx = -3y\n  check: 3 + (-3) = 0    OK\n\nNOTE: psi needs 2-D + incompressible.\n      It does NOT need irrotational.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.5, pp.180-184 (8th ed.).' },
