        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'LAMINAR FLOW BETWEEN PARALLEL PLATES\n\nCASE 1 - PLANE POISEUILLE (both plates fixed,\n         pressure driven):\n\n  u(y) = (dp/dx)/(2*mu) * ( y^2 - h*y )   PARABOLA\n  q    = (dp/dx) * h^3 / (12*mu)          per unit width\n\n  q goes as h^3 - double the gap, EIGHT times the flow\n\nCASE 2 - COUETTE (no pressure gradient, top plate\n         moving at U):\n\n  u(y) = U * y / h                        STRAIGHT LINE\n\n  ^ this is exactly the case assumed when the\n    Newtonian shear law was introduced in Module 1\n\nGENERAL CASE = CASE 1 + CASE 2 (equation is LINEAR)\n\n  favourable dp/dx -> profile BULGES forward\n  zero dp/dx       -> straight line\n  adverse  dp/dx   -> FLOW REVERSES near the fixed wall\n                      ^ preview of SEPARATION, Module 4\n\nWORKED: mu=0.15, h=5 mm, dp/dx=1200 Pa/m, both fixed\n\n  q = 1200 * (0.005)^3 / (12*0.15) = 8.33e-5 m^3/s per m\n  V_mean = q/h = 0.0167 m/s\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.8, pp.332-344 (8th ed.).' },
