        dryRun: {
          input: 'Air at 300 kelvin and 100 kilopascals. Find its density, specific heats and the speed of sound.',
          steps: [
            'Density is pressure divided by gas constant and temperature, that is 100000 divided by 287 multiplied by 300, giving 1.161 kilograms per cubic metre',
            'The specific heat at constant pressure is gamma multiplied by the gas constant divided by gamma minus one, that is 1.4 times 287 divided by 0.4, giving 1004.5 joules per kilogram kelvin',
            'The specific heat at constant volume is that divided by gamma, giving 717.5',
            'The speed of sound is the square root of gamma multiplied by the gas constant and temperature',
          ],
          result: 'A speed of sound of 347 metres per second. Note that every quantity depends on temperature and none on pressure, which is the first indication that temperature is the controlling variable throughout this module.',
        },
        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'THERMODYNAMIC GROUNDWORK\n\nPERFECT GAS:\n\n  p = rho * R * T           R_air = 287 J/kg.K\n  ALWAYS absolute p and absolute T. No exceptions.\n\nENERGY:\n\n  u = c_v * T          internal energy\n  h = u + p/rho = c_p * T     enthalpy\n\n  c_p - c_v = R\n  gamma = c_p / c_v = 1.4 for air\n\n  c_p = gamma*R/(gamma-1) = 1004.5 J/kg.K\n  c_v = R/(gamma-1)       =  717.5 J/kg.K\n\nISENTROPIC RELATIONS (adiabatic + reversible):\n\n  p / rho^gamma = constant\n  T / p^((gamma-1)/gamma) = constant\n\nENTROPY - the admissibility test:\n\n  ds = c_p*ln(T2/T1) - R*ln(p2/p1)\n\n  adiabatic process:  ds >= 0 REQUIRED\n  ds < 0 -> the process CANNOT HAPPEN\n\n  ^ this single rule is what forbids the expansion shock.\n\nWORKED: air, 300 K, 100 kPa\n  rho = 100000/(287*300) = 1.161 kg/m^3\n  a   = sqrt(1.4*287*300) = 347 m/s\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.12, pp.659-665 (8th ed.).' },
