        code: { lang: 'text', src: 'SPEED OF SOUND\n\nControl volume riding with the wave -> steady flow:\n\n  continuity:  rho*a = (rho+drho)*(a - dV)\n  momentum  :  dp    = rho*a*dV\n\n  eliminate dV:\n\n    a^2 = dp/drho   at CONSTANT ENTROPY\n\nFOR A PERFECT GAS (isentropic, p/rho^gamma = const):\n\n  a = sqrt( gamma * R * T )\n\n  DEPENDS ON TEMPERATURE ALONE.\n  NOT on pressure. NOT on density separately.\n\nFOR A LIQUID:  a = sqrt( K / rho )    K = bulk modulus\n\n  water: sqrt(2.2e9/1000) = 1483 m/s\n  ^ the SAME calculation made in Module 1.\n\nWORKED: aircraft at 250 m/s, T = -50 C = 223 K\n\n  a = sqrt(1.4*287*223) = 299 m/s\n  M = 250/299 = 0.836\n\n  same airspeed at sea level (288 K, a = 340):\n  M = 250/340 = 0.735\n\n  Airspeed unchanged. ONLY the temperature changed.\n  This is why altitude matters for a transonic aircraft.\n\nSOURCE: TB1 Ch.12, pp.665-673 (8th ed.).' },
