        definition:
          'The Mach number is the ratio of the local flow speed to the local speed of sound, and it classifies compressible flow into regimes: incompressible in effect below 0.3, subsonic to 0.8, transonic to 1.2, supersonic beyond that and hypersonic above about 5. Its physical meaning is about information. A disturbance spreads at the speed of sound, so in subsonic flow the disturbance outruns the body and the flow ahead is warned of its approach, while in supersonic flow the body outruns its own signals and the disturbances pile up into a cone behind it. Outside that Mach cone lies a zone of silence in which the presence of the body is completely unknown.',
